(TCPC relocated-sphere loaded-candidate recovery - T4 long probe.)
(Dedicated campaign 2026082404 mode 27 attempt 3; frozen R2 candidate.)
(No WCS changes. No G43/G49 changes. TCPC must already be ON.)

(Operator setup:)
(1. After relocating and securing the sphere, start at the operator-confirmed)
(   T4 B0/C0 point 3-5 mm above it. Apply G43 H4 before G43.4.)
(2. Keep hand on feed hold/stop for the full first run.)
(3. This exact file is frozen to mode 27, attempt 3, campaign 2026082404.)
(4. It records 66 rows: a fresh B0 reference; the complete B-15 block;)
(   then original sequences 52-101. Sequences 10-44 are deliberately absent.)
(5. Sphere-to-post direction remains X- Y+ Z-.)
(6. Run only from the separate candidate diagnostic INI after its offline)
(   configuration, program, pose, hash, and reachability preflight passes.)
(7. This runner installs the frozen T4 #3032 value before probing.)
(8. Outside-G38 probe activity never pauses; each G38 requires clear inputs.)
(9. Each pose uses W, the sign-aware upper U side, -V, and +V.)
(10. Low B adds C45/C225; B30 and higher remain on C quadrants.)
(11. C135/C315 remain excluded known collision sectors near the post.)

(Accepted recovery rows log only to:)
(/home/cnc5/linuxcnc-dev/configs/5th_axis_xyzbc_ssi_tcpc_probe_basic/tcpc-relocated-sphere-t4-candidate-r2-attempt3-recovery-results.csv)
(State logs only to tcpc-relocated-sphere-t4-candidate-r2-attempt3-recovery-state.csv.)
(Every G38 transaction logs counters to the dedicated attempt3 recovery)
(contact trace. Counter snapshots add diagnostics; they do not alter motion.)
(A second gap trace accounts for every sticky edge between one contact's)
(release-ready snapshot and the next G38 pre-contact snapshot.)

G21 G17 G40 G64 P0.001 G80 G90 G94

o<preview_guard> if [#<_task> EQ 0]
  (DEBUG, TCPC_RELOCATED_SPHERE_T4_CANDIDATE_R2 preview only)
  M2
o<preview_guard> endif

(The TCPC HAL gates motion.probe-input only from real-time G38 motion type.)
(Clear legacy digital requests; this runner does not drive either physical gate.)
